==Strategy==
The main and preferred strategy for this stage is to steamroll Yulala with extreme amounts of damage before the nasty peons get in the way, as the battle only gets worse when Miz Devil (whose shield protects her from status effects) joins the fray. Otherwise, players are advised to stick an endurance strategy, which involves deploying CC units that can consistently stall Yulala or whatever that counters the peons. Feel free to bring any Uber that could be helpful. A Rich Cat is practically mandatory, as there are little to no sources of funds.

Even though Lowkey may present a threat, he's too slow to support Yulala, whose defeat effectively wins you the stage, as Idi:N has no trouble killing Lowkey with Doron's help.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi]] - The essence of many strategies, Idi is a short-ranged rusher with a decently low cooldown (~91 seconds), deals massive damage to relics, is curse immune and can survive a Yulala hit when over level 37 (30750>30000). Idi's damage exceeds 200,000 at level 40, and can reach an insane '''354,375''' (which is just a few thousand points shy of knocking back Yulala) at level 50 with the best attack [[Cat Combo|combos]] in the entire game (+25% damage) for players who have cleared [[Revival of Origin]]. Even at level 40 with more accessible combos (+20% damage), she is still able to deal a whopping '''277,200''' damage per hit. Obviously, her only weaknesses are peons getting in her way, low range (175) and very low health. This makes any strategy revolving her incredibly difficult without meticulous timing and assorted support, but when used well, can possibly raze the stage. After Yulala is gone, Idi can be used to kill Lowkey, again only with support.
*[[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Doron]] - Doron is a primarily anti-relic CC unit who can disable them for several seconds, and his True Form even has knockback to recover ground. Aside from having extreme health, Doron also has immunity to warp and curse, ensuring he will almost always hit Yulala. Doron's cooldown is somewhat long (~1 minute), so he has to be used where it counts, such as to let Idi get one more hit in which can make all the difference. Doron also comes in handy when dealing with Lowkey.
*[[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train]] - Bullet Train works just as well as it did in [[Heavenly Tower/Floor 40|Heavenly Tower]], able to survive a Yulala hit at level 50. It is especially useful in rush strategies to get some chip damage, and possibly supplement Idi with its lower overall cooldown.
*[[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Mohawk]]/[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone]] - Due to how Yulala's warp works, slow meatshields are out of the picture. Manic Mohawk is cheap and can reach Yulala quickly, while Stone (if boosted by research combos), with its absolutely massive health and warp immunity, will prevent Yulala from pushing and bait one more attack, while stalling peons. Idi chain strategies are heavily reliant on such sources of consistent meatshielding, as knocking Yulala back allows her to barely avoid his Omni Strike.
*[[Crazed Cow Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Lion]] - For dealing with Croconators and stopping Yulala in the event of an emergency.
*[[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Deadeye]]/[[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk]] - For players comfortable with an endurance battle and can deal with the peons, they are able to slow Yulala and gradually chip him at range.
*[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Slime]] - A more common solution to the peons while also abusing them to fire its wave and chip Yulala. Its high damage helps crippling Miz Devil and Relic Doge.
*[[Ancient Egg: N000 (Special Cat)|Ape Lord Luza]] - Although Ape Lord Luza does not outrange Yulala (400 range), it has massive damage and resistance to Relics. It is also immune to curse and warp, allowing it to stand for itself temporarily.
*[[Dogumaru (Special Cat)|Reborn Warrior Doguemon]] - Being resistant to Relic and immune to warp/curse, Reborn Warrior Doguemon is an excellent option to hold off Yulala briefly while doing decent damage, and can also deal with Relic Doge. Unfortunately, this unit struggles when other peons arrive, so it must be backed by meatshields and attackers nevertheless. While it doesn't have too much uptime, its reduced recharge time means it can keep up more comfortably.
*[[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Esoteric Uril]] - Esoteric Uril is a very useful unit on future replays if [[Infernal Tower/Floor 50|his stage]] has been cleared beforehand. Being Strong Against Relics and Aku with Curse/Slow and Immunity to Curse, Uril's Surges can exploit Yulala's low standing range of 200 to greatly impede him, and disable his Warp ability, all while absorbing and dishing out substantial amounts of damage. In the case of a loss, Uril is fairly easy to replace if used properly.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Tecoluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Lufalan Pasalan]] - Lufalan Pasalan has 720 range, allowing it to comfortably deal with Yulala. At level 50 without talents, it does nearly 200,000 damage in a single hit, and if things go awry, has enough health to survive and reposition once. Its critical hit isn't consistent, but can tremendously speed up the fight when it occurs. The only problem with it is the fast pace of the stage, meaning it must be spawned immediately at the start before the peons can interfere.
*[[Balaluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Piccolan Pasalan]] - Piccolan acts similar to Cyberpunk, supplementing attackers at extreme range (900) with a 3-second freeze and a 6-second weaken in exchange for having low damage. Piccolan certainly doesn't work alone and is best suited for endurance approaches, but is a great addition to any associated strategies.
*[[Asiluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Assassinlan Pasalan]] - Assassinlan's brief 3-second slow at 1250 range makes it near-identical to Cyberpunk without the blindspot. The absolutely massive coverage allows Assassinlan to essentially slow every enemy on the field at once. The effect is brief, but it does pay off when used alongside other crowd-controllers to ensure the enemies can never push far. It is especially useful if Cyberpunk is included, as they can potentially cover each other's downtime.
*[[Trixi the Merc (Uber Rare Cat)|Trixi the Revenant]] - Given her [[Strong Against|Strong VS]] Relics, as well as her various abilities and immunities, Trixi is extraordinarily well-suited for this stage. She is capable of tanking various hits from the boss, while subsequently stalling him with her stutter [[Freeze]]. Her matchup with the peons is equally as impressive, reducing the Croconators, Relic Doges, and Trolly Bloggers to ashes in less than a second. The only enemy you need to protect her against is the Miz Devils which can, and will, drain her HP pool at an alarming rate.
*[[Child of Destiny Phono (Uber Rare Cat)|King of Destiny Phonoa]] - Massive damage to traited enemies, 600 standing range with a three-part multi-hit that improves his overall consistency, be it against the peons or Yulala. Having LD attacks also allow it to simply bypass Croconators without fear of obstruction.
*[[King of Doom Phono (Uber Rare Cat)|King of Extinction Phono]] - This unit has a level 1 Mini-Surge, a very brief 2-second slow effect against all enemies and provides support with their closely-spaced LD Multi-Hits from extreme range (stands at 550, hits up to 900) that can hit much further behind Yulala. Despite their DPS, they are best used supportively, as their slow uptime is rather low.
*[[Hades the Punisher (Uber Rare Cat)|Almighty Hades]] - Having Warp Immunity and massive health, Hades can be used to temporarily tank a number of Yulala hits and keep him there, with enough damage to chip the peons at well. However, his extreme cooldown leaves much to be desired compared to specialist tanks.
*[[Talents|Talented]] [[Gravi (Uber Rare Cat)|Gravolodon]] - With its target Relic Talent and given its [[Immune to Warp|Warp Immunity]], it can completely stall Yulala with little trouble. Not only that, Gravolodon does decent damage, just be sure to protect it from the peons.
*[[Celestial Child Luna (Uber Rare Cat)|Salvation's Daughter Lunacia]] - Despite not outranging Yulala's [[Omni Strike]] or having Warp Immunity, she can still be put to great use with a stepping stone or timed with the Thunderbolt cannon. She can clear peons, and with her Strong VS and Freeze against Relic, deal good damage and temporarily disable Yulala and Lowkey. Even without a stepping stone, she can either exploit Yulala's low range or get a few lucky hits in, especially with [[Sniper the Cat|either]] [[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper]] interrupting Yulala's attacks, relieving pressure, and her cooldown means she can be replaced quickly if dead.

